{"id": "swebq0069", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 369509382, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "3d4d39fcc4a346fd8580c0316523f086cfbea87a1efa8a46667c283f61f94b66", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 NVL", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "what led to stalin rise in power?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0069.wav", "input_sha256": "9c9d1bd1d6699469011b26fa32cfe99e82f98ea206b2a6b14cd906ac2ed335c2", "input_samples": 37134, "input_s": 2.321, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.5955, "act": 0.996, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "He was the general secretary of the party. He had been a military officer, so he had a lot of authority and power within the party. And then when Lenin died in 19 24, he became the leader of the Soviet Union. He was very ambitious and wanted to make sure that he could control everything around him. So he started purging people who were not loyal to him or who had different ideas than him. He also believed in collectivization, which meant taking all the land from the peasants and giving it to the state. This caused a lot of problems for the Soviet economy because they didn't have enough food to feed everyone. But he kept pushing forward with his plans, even though things weren' t going well. Eventually, he became known as one of the most brutal leaders in history.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 34, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0069_local_local.wav", "sha256": "34a04e318cc06d8722f50566cda209b6d7f4